HST Office: Writer's Styles gallery as in the approved 1.0.2 mockup, and the ribbon's font boxes 128 and 46 px wide.

The gallery was a blank strip on gtk3 whenever it showed (2400 px, rc 3f3a7555): HstApplyPreviews() set the
scrolled window's size request to (width, -1), which drops the .ui's height-request, and with external scroll bars
the view kept only its 2 px frame, so its previews were cut away (seen in the accessibility tree: the scroll pane
784 x 2 px holding 7 previews). On Windows vcl's builder makes the icon view its own scrolled window, so
"stylesscroll" does not exist there and the gallery kept the .ui's one preview: the view takes the size itself
now, and a preview's image leaves vcl's own 5 px around it (86 x 64; gtk: 92 x 70 and the item padding 2).

Now the gallery has one-line previews of 96 x 74 px in a 1 px frame, and a 16 px column of ˄ ˅ ▾ (previous row, next
row, all styles); it keeps 6, 4 or 3 previews at the large, medium and small ribbon state, n x 96 + 2 + 16 px, and
never takes the room the ribbon leaves (the page no longer follows the view width). After a state change the
item window's cached content requisition is invalidated before it is measured, or the ladder saw the large
gallery's width at every state. A common Writer style shows its
short name (Thường, Văn bản, Tiêu đề 1, Tiêu đề 2, Tựa đề, Trích dẫn; svx/inc/hststylesshortnames.hrc) in its own
font and colour, and those six come first; the styles keep their names in the document, and the tooltip and the
accessible name stay the full name. In Calc the same gallery (.uno:StylesPreview; the style family Para is
Calc's cell styles) shows cell styles as cells, their fill or white in a light grey frame, in the Sheets mockup's
order: Default, Good, Neutral, Bad, Warning, Heading 1, then Heading 2, Note, Accent 1-3, Result
(StylesPreviewToolBoxControl.cxx); previews are cached per module, and a preview's font height is read in its
pool's unit (Calc's twips, not the shell's 1/100 mm). In a notebookbar the font name box is 128 px
and the font size box 46 px (svx/source/inc/HstRibbonCombos.hxx): the part of the box's preferred width over
the target is taken off its request, once when it is made and once more after it is first shown (on gtk3 the
▾ button is counted only then: 128 px became 165). In the ribbon both boxes are made from fontnameboxribbon.ui /
fontsizeboxribbon.ui, whose combo box has the class "hst-ribbon-combo": vcl gtk3 then narrows the side padding of
its entry (4 / 2 px) and drop-down button (2 px), frames kept, so Adwaita's size box reaches 46 px with "12" still
readable (its entry keeps two characters; the owner's decision D9). Toolbars, the sidebar and dialogs keep their
boxes, widths and the theme's padding. The ribbon's size box shows "12", not "12 pt" (owner's decision): svtools
FontSizeBox::set_show_unit(false), a flag in the byte of its other flags so the class keeps its layout; typing
"12" or "12 pt" still works, and dialogs, the sidebar and toolbars keep the unit.

